# Copy this file to .env. Sign-in is done by hand in a browser window
# (run `python -m deepseek.auth` or `python -m qwen.auth`), so no credentials are stored here.
# All providers are opt-in. DeepSeek web automation may restrict your account.
DEEPSEEK_ENABLED=0
# Minimum seconds between attempts/continuations per provider in one process.
# This is pacing, not a guarantee of acceptable use or website quota.
PROVIDER_MIN_INTERVAL=10
# Optional Qwen Chat models: run `python -m qwen.auth`, then set QWEN_ENABLED=1.
# Qwen uses a separate profile and session under session/qwen/.
QWEN_ENABLED=0
# QWEN_PROFILE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/a/dedicated/qwen/profile

# Experimental signed-in browser tabs (Safari Userscripts or a compatible manager).
# Read browser/README.md before enabling. Each uses the web UI's selected model.
BROWSER_BRIDGE_ENABLED=0
GROK_ENABLED=0
MISTRAL_ENABLED=0
KIMI_ENABLED=0
GLM_ENABLED=0
# WEB_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT=180

# Gemini uses the official Antigravity CLI, with tools disabled.
# Sign in with `agy`; obtain real account model slugs with `agy models`.
GEMINI_ENABLED=0
GEMINI_MODELS={}
# ANTIGRAVITY_BIN=agy
# For a broken IPv6 socket only, providers.antigravity_ipv4 wraps the official
# CLI using IPv4 on your existing route, without changing system/VPN settings.

# --- Optional ---
# DEEPSEEK_PROFILE_DIR=session/profile   # reuse an existing signed-in Chrome profile
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8000
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=30               # per-client-IP limit on /v1 endpoints

# Sessions are loaded from cache only. The server never logs in, refreshes a
# browser session in the background, or replays a rejected request.
# Missing/expired sessions return 401 login_required, or a terminal SSE error
# after streaming headers are sent. Run the auth CLI manually.
# Restrictions, quota and uncertain upstream failures pause that provider in
# session/provider-pauses.json (HTTP 403; SSE error if headers are already sent).
# Inspect: python -m providers.access status
# After confirming normal website access manually:
#   python -m providers.access resume qwen
# Existing SERVER_INTERACTIVE_LOGIN / SESSION_REFRESH_ENABLED settings no longer
# enable automatic browser capture in the server.

# --- Tool-call truncation handling ---
# DeepSeek's web output limit can cut a large tool call off mid-JSON. When that
# happens the bridge resumes the same thread and asks the model to continue,
# concatenating slices until the entire fenced tool_calls array validates.
# Partial calls are never returned. Set how many continuations to try (>=0).
# TOOLCALL_MAX_CONTINUATIONS=3

# Dump the raw model reply to the log whenever a tool call can't be parsed.
# DEBUG_TOOLCALLS=1
